*> vybe-test: cobol/alphabet_clause/alphabet_clause_multiple_alphabets_runtime
*> origin: languages/cobol/tests/cobol/test_alphabet_clause.rs

IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. ALPHA18.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
CONFIGURATION SECTION.
SPECIAL-NAMES.
    ALPHABET ALPHA-LOW IS "a" THRU "z".
    ALPHABET ALPHA-UPPER IS "A" THRU "Z".
    COLLATING SEQUENCE IS ALPHA-LOW.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 WS-VYBE-L PIC X(256).
01 WS-LOW  PIC X VALUE "b".
01 WS-UPER PIC X VALUE "A".
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    IF WS-LOW < WS-UPER
        DISPLAY "LOWER-FIRST"
    END-IF.
    MOVE SPACES TO WS-VYBE-L
    STRING "LOWER-FIRST" DELIMITED SIZE INTO WS-VYBE-L
    IF WS-VYBE-L NOT = "LOWER-FIRST"
        DISPLAY "FAIL: want [LOWER-FIRST] got [" WS-VYBE-L "]"
        MOVE 1 TO RETURN-CODE
        RAISE EXCEPTION EC-PROGRAM
    END-IF.
    STOP RUN.

